Here is the full **testsmells.org 19-smell academic audit** of `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`.

---

## Integration-Test Calibration Note

The class is annotated `[TestCategory("Integration")]`. Per the academic calibration rules, **Mystery Guest** and **Eager Test** severity are downgraded for integration tests. This suite correctly uses an in-memory SQLite database (hermetic), so no Mystery Guest finding applies. No method exceeds the 4+ distinct production method threshold for Eager Test either.

---

## Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

## Findings by Severity

### 🔴 HIGH — 1. Assertion-Free Test (a.k.a. Unknown Test)

**Affected:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)

```csharp
// No assertion anywhere — passes even if every Insert silently fails
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
}
```

**Risk:** False confidence — 100 % coverage, 0 % verification.

**Fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count, "All bulk-inserted users should be persisted.");
}
```

---

### 🔴 HIGH — 2. Conditional Test Logic

**Affected:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 93)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Risk:** One branch is never exercised (you inserted a plain `User`, so the `PremiumUser` path is dead code). The test silently asserts only the else branch — the `PremiumUser` check is never validated.

**Fix:** Split into two explicit tests:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("vip@example.com", "VIP", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("vip@example.com")!;

    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0, "Premium user should have a positive discount rate.");
}
```

---

### 🔴 HIGH — 3. Sleepy Test

**Affected:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);   // 3-second hard wait
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Risk:** Non-deterministic (3 s may not be enough under load), and unconditionally slows the suite by 3 s. Even in integration tests, `Thread.Sleep` is a smell — the calibration rules note it should still be flagged.

**Fix:** Use a polling/retry helper with a timeout:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var sent = await WaitUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent, "Notification should be sent after insert.");
}

private static async Task<bool> WaitUntilAsync(Func<bool> condition, TimeSpan timeout)
{
    var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow + timeout;
    while (DateTime.UtcNow < deadline)
    {
        if (condition()) return true;
        await Task.Delay(100);
    }
    return false;
}
```

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — 4. Assertion Roulette

**Affected:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);          // which one failed?
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

4 assertions, zero message parameters. When one fails in CI, the runner reports a line number but no human-readable explanation.

**Fix:** Add message parameters:
